concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 State laws may operate concurrently"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This Act is not intended to exclude the operation of any State law, to the extent that the State law is capable of operating concurrently with this Act, other than a State law prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this section. (2) The Governor-General may prescribe a State law under subsection (1) only if: (a) there is no corresponding State law in effect in relation to that State; and (b) either: (i) the State law relates specifically to dealings with GMOs; or (ii) for the purposes of a decision under the State law as to whether or not a licence, authority or approval (however described) is granted under the State law, the State law distinguishes between dealings with GMOs and dealings with other things." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This Act is not intended to exclude the operation of any State law, to the extent that the State law is capable of operating concurrently with this Act, other than a State law prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this section. (2) The Governor-General may prescribe a State law under subsection (1) only if: (a) there is no corresponding State law in effect in relation to that State; and (b) either: (i) the State law relates specifically to dealings with GMOs; or (ii) for the purposes of a decision under the State law as to whether or not a licence, authority or approval (however described) is granted under the State law, the State law distinguishes between dealings with GMOs and dealings with other things."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b9fbacd3e9a37c9f539608d164a7780b418756129468254a8f173a23d5220c16" ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
