doc:sec-35a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "35A(2) Person must not breach conditions of emergency dealing" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An offence under this section is punishable on conviction by whichever of the following applies:   Regulation of dealings with GMOs  Part 4 Dealings with GMOs must be licensed  Division 2 Section 35B Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024 (a) in the case of an aggravated offence—imprisonment for 5 years or 2,000 penalty units; (b) in any other case—imprisonment for 2 years or 500 penalty units. Note: Section 38 defines aggravated offence." ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer .

concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-35b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35B Person must not breach conditions of emergency dealing"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-35b ;
    values:originalText "determination—strict liability offence (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person takes an action or omits to take an action; and (b) the person has knowledge of the conditions to which an emergency dealing determination is subject; and (c) the action or omission by the person contravenes such a condition. Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility. (2) Strict liability applies to paragraphs (1)(a) and (c). Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. (3) An offence under this section is punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than whichever of the following amounts applies: (a) in the case of an aggravated offence—200 penalty units; (b) in any other case—50 penalty units. Note: Section 38 defines aggravated offence." ;
    skos:definition "determination—strict liability offence (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person takes an action or omits to take an action; and (b) the person has knowledge of the conditions to which an emergency dealing determination is subject; and (c) the action or omission by the person contravenes such a condition. Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility. (2) Strict liability applies to paragraphs (1)(a) and (c). Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. (3) An offence under this section is punishable on conviction by a fine of not more than whichever of the following amounts applies: (a) in the case of an aggravated offence—200 penalty units; (b) in any other case—50 penalty units. Note: Section 38 defines aggravated offence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1b06f60b814481d4a3ede782a0e1b208fac94c41c8d05f12b630aa995a9dbb00" ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer ;
