concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-38 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "38 Aggravated offences—significant damage to health or safety of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-38 ;
    values:originalText "people or to the environment (1) An offence is an aggravated offence if the commission of the offence causes significant damage, or is likely to cause significant damage, to the health and safety of people or to the environment. (2) In order to prove an aggravated offence, the prosecution must prove that the person who committed the offence: (a) intended his or her conduct to cause significant damage to the health and safety of people or to the environment; or (b) was reckless as to whether that conduct would cause significant damage to the health and safety of people or to the environment.   Licensing system  Part 5 Simplified outline  Division 1 Section 39 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024" ;
    skos:definition "people or to the environment (1) An offence is an aggravated offence if the commission of the offence causes significant damage, or is likely to cause significant damage, to the health and safety of people or to the environment. (2) In order to prove an aggravated offence, the prosecution must prove that the person who committed the offence: (a) intended his or her conduct to cause significant damage to the health and safety of people or to the environment; or (b) was reckless as to whether that conduct would cause significant damage to the health and safety of people or to the environment.   Licensing system  Part 5 Simplified outline  Division 1 Section 39 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2db38e115c09be890fe3421ad5d4febc998af1a452425333b26254e9f55c3f6e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-38-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-38-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <gene-technology-act-2000.pdf> ;
    dc:source "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.40" .
doc:sec-38 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "38 Aggravated offences—significant damage to health or safety of" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "people or to the environment (1) An offence is an aggravated offence if the commission of the offence causes significant damage, or is likely to cause significant damage, to the health and safety of people or to the environment. (2) In order to prove an aggravated offence, the prosecution must prove that the person who committed the offence: (a) intended his or her conduct to cause significant damage to the health and safety of people or to the environment; or (b) was reckless as to whether that conduct would cause significant damage to the health and safety of people or to the environment.   Licensing system  Part 5 Simplified outline  Division 1 Section 39 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer .

