concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-42 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42 Regulator may require applicant to give further information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Regulator may, by notice in writing, require an applicant for a licence to give the Regulator such further information in relation to the application as the Regulator requires. (2) The notice may specify the period within which the information is to be provided. (3) The Regulator may require information to be given under this section at any time before the Regulator decides the application, whether before or after the Regulator has begun to consider the application." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Regulator may, by notice in writing, require an applicant for a licence to give the Regulator such further information in relation to the application as the Regulator requires. (2) The notice may specify the period within which the information is to be provided. (3) The Regulator may require information to be given under this section at any time before the Regulator decides the application, whether before or after the Regulator has begun to consider the application."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a4ebc5a966a71b556ee30e2827f965f6cbd099188ca4d3f447c415c8db04b4d9" ;
