    cof:title "58(3) Matters to be taken into account in deciding whether a person is" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) In this section: relevant conviction means a conviction for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a foreign country, being a law relating to the health and safety of people or the environment, if: (a) the offence was committed within the period of 10 years immediately before the making of the application for the licence; and (b) the offence was punishable on conviction by a fine of $5,000 or more, or by a term of imprisonment of one year or more." ;
