concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-60 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "60 Period of licence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-60 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A licence continues in force: (a) if the licence is expressed to be in force for a particular period—until the end of that period; or (b) otherwise—until it is cancelled or surrendered. (2) A licence is not in force throughout any period of suspension. (3) A licence issued as a result of an inadvertent dealings application must not be expressed to be in force for a period of longer than 12 months.   Licensing system  Part 5 Conditions of licences  Division 6 Section 61 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A licence continues in force: (a) if the licence is expressed to be in force for a particular period—until the end of that period; or (b) otherwise—until it is cancelled or surrendered. (2) A licence is not in force throughout any period of suspension. (3) A licence issued as a result of an inadvertent dealings application must not be expressed to be in force for a period of longer than 12 months.   Licensing system  Part 5 Conditions of licences  Division 6 Section 61 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d036e7a17c362f2c4536f8848edad5a96b1cf3620bcfb66a69173102d49302d6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-60-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-60-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-60-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
