concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72c-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "72C(5) Period of effect of emergency dealing determination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-72c-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) The Minister may extend the period of effect of an emergency dealing determination only if: (a) the Minister has received advice from the original adviser in relation to the emergency dealing determination that the threat to which the determination relates still exists, and that the proposed extension would, or would be likely to, adequately address the threat; and (b) the Minister is satisfied that the threat still exists, and that the proposed extension would, or would be likely to, adequately address that threat; and (c) the Minister has received advice from the Regulator that any risks posed by the proposed extension are able to be managed in such a way as: (i) to protect the health and safety of people; and (ii) to protect the environment; and (d) the Minister is satisfied that any risks posed by the proposed extension are able to be managed in such a way as: (i) to protect the health and safety of people; and (ii) to protect the environment; and (e) a majority of jurisdictions agree to the extension." ;
    skos:definition "(5) The Minister may extend the period of effect of an emergency dealing determination only if: (a) the Minister has received advice from the original adviser in relation to the emergency dealing determination that the threat to which the determination relates still exists, and that the proposed extension would, or would be likely to, adequately address the threat; and (b) the Minister is satisfied that the threat still exists, and that the proposed extension would, or would be likely to, adequately address that threat; and (c) the Minister has received advice from the Regulator that any risks posed by the proposed extension are able to be managed in such a way as: (i) to protect the health and safety of people; and (ii) to protect the environment; and (d) the Minister is satisfied that any risks posed by the proposed extension are able to be managed in such a way as: (i) to protect the health and safety of people; and (ii) to protect the environment; and (e) a majority of jurisdictions agree to the extension."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2b58918d73f6b892eafb4d68f1cd1051103d3b30a1bfa0b524320622bbcf7903" ;
    values:partOf concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-72c ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Minister may extend the period of effect of an emergency dealing determination under certain conditions." ;
