doc:sec-100-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "100(4) The Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) Before appointing a member of the Committee, the Minister must consult the following: (a) the States; (b) the Regulator; (c) such scientific, consumer, health, environmental and industry groups as the Minister considers appropriate; (d) such other Ministers as the Minister considers appropriate." ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer .

concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-100-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "100(5) The Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-100-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Subject to subsections (6) and (7A), the Minister must not appoint a person as a member of the Committee unless the Minister is satisfied that the person has skills or experience in one or more of the following areas: (a) molecular biology; (b) ecology; (c) plant, microbial, animal or human genetics; (d) virology; (e) entomology; (f) agricultural or aquacultural systems; (g) biosafety engineering; (h) public health; (i) occupational health and safety; (j) risk assessment;   The Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and the Gene Technology Ethics and Community Consultative Committee  Part 8 The Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee  Division 2 Section 101 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024 (k) clinical medicine; (l) biochemistry; (m) pharmacology; (n) plant or animal pathology; (o) botany; (p) microbiology; (q) animal biology; (r) immunology; (s) toxicology; (t) an area specified by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph." ;
    skos:definition "(5) Subject to subsections (6) and (7A), the Minister must not appoint a person as a member of the Committee unless the Minister is satisfied that the person has skills or experience in one or more of the following areas: (a) molecular biology; (b) ecology; (c) plant, microbial, animal or human genetics; (d) virology; (e) entomology; (f) agricultural or aquacultural systems; (g) biosafety engineering; (h) public health; (i) occupational health and safety; (j) risk assessment;   The Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee and the Gene Technology Ethics and Community Consultative Committee  Part 8 The Gene Technology Technical Advisory Committee  Division 2 Section 101 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024 (k) clinical medicine; (l) biochemistry; (m) pharmacology; (n) plant or animal pathology; (o) botany; (p) microbiology; (q) animal biology; (r) immunology; (s) toxicology; (t) an area specified by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d27c814c2fa947150a1923efd275ddec2579aeed0c31a5d436c70659483c4a4c" ;
    values:partOf concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-100 ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Minister must have skills or experience in one or more of the specified areas before appointing a person as a member of the Committee." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <gene-technology-act-2000.pdf> ;
    dc:source "gene-technology-act-2000.pdf, p.94" ;
