doc:sec-154-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "154(3) Searches and seizures related to offences" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If: (a) in the course of searching, in accordance with a warrant, for a particular thing, an inspector finds another thing that the inspector believes on reasonable grounds to be evidential material; and (b) the inspector believes, on reasonable grounds, that it is necessary to seize that other thing in order to prevent its concealment, loss or destruction, or its use in committing, continuing or repeating an offence against this Act or the regulations; the warrant is taken to authorise the inspector to seize that other thing." ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer .

concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-155 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "155 Offence-related powers of inspectors in relation to premises"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-155 ;
    values:originalText "The powers an inspector may exercise under paragraph 154(2)(b) are as follows: (a) to search the premises and any thing on the premises for the evidential material; (b) to inspect, examine, take measurements of, conduct tests on, or take samples of the evidential material;   Powers of inspection  Part 11 Offence-related powers  Division 4 Section 156 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024 (c) to take photographs, make video or audio recordings or make sketches of the premises or the evidential material; (d) to take onto the premises such equipment and materials as the inspector requires for the purpose of exercising powers in relation to the premises." ;
    skos:definition "The powers an inspector may exercise under paragraph 154(2)(b) are as follows: (a) to search the premises and any thing on the premises for the evidential material; (b) to inspect, examine, take measurements of, conduct tests on, or take samples of the evidential material;   Powers of inspection  Part 11 Offence-related powers  Division 4 Section 156 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024 (c) to take photographs, make video or audio recordings or make sketches of the premises or the evidential material; (d) to take onto the premises such equipment and materials as the inspector requires for the purpose of exercising powers in relation to the premises."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3d400308fe0498dfba8e4b42659aef87cd742f58220a7ec66575872e1515305b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Inspector's powers of search, inspection, and sampling" ;
