concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-180 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "180 Notification of decisions and review rights"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-180 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Regulator must, as soon as practicable after making a reviewable decision, cause a notice in writing to be given to each eligible person in relation to the decision, containing: (a) the terms of the decision; and (b) the reasons for the decision; and (c) a statement setting out particulars of the person’s review rights.   Miscellaneous  Part 12 Review of decisions  Division 2 Section 181 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024 (2) A failure to comply with the requirements of subsection (1) in relation to a decision does not affect the validity of the decision." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Regulator must, as soon as practicable after making a reviewable decision, cause a notice in writing to be given to each eligible person in relation to the decision, containing: (a) the terms of the decision; and (b) the reasons for the decision; and (c) a statement setting out particulars of the person’s review rights.   Miscellaneous  Part 12 Review of decisions  Division 2 Section 181 Gene Technology Act 2000 Compilation date: 14/10/2024 (2) A failure to comply with the requirements of subsection (1) in relation to a decision does not affect the validity of the decision."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "399acebd9a3af4594a3b83cc99475e71003a7cf6510d94b96f13945b65a216ec" ;
    cof:pageNumber "148"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-180-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:gene-technology-act-2000-sec-180-ss-2 ;
